    <CAT value="General remote services" port="22" protocol="tcp">
      <INFO number="38047" severity="1">
        <TITLE><![CDATA[SSH daemon information retrieving]]></TITLE>
        <LAST_UPDATE><![CDATA[2009-04-21T18:50:05Z]]></LAST_UPDATE>
        <PCI_FLAG>0</PCI_FLAG>
        <CVE_ID_LIST>
          <CVE_ID>
            <ID><![CDATA[CVE-1999-0634]]></ID>
            <URL><![CDATA[http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-1999-0634]]></URL>
          </CVE_ID>
        </CVE_ID_LIST>
        <DIAGNOSIS><![CDATA[SSH is a secure protocol, provided it is fully patched, properly configured, and uses FIPS approved algorithms. 
<P>
<PRE>
For Red Hat ES 4:-
SSH1 supported					yes
Supported authentification methods for SSH1	RSA,password
Supported ciphers for SSH1			3des,blowfish
