        <LAST_UPDATE><![CDATA[2016-04-28T03:30:16Z]]></LAST_UPDATE>
        <PCI_FLAG>1</PCI_FLAG>
        <DIAGNOSIS><![CDATA[A remote management service that accepts unencrypted credentials was detected on target host.
<P>
Services like Telnet, FTP, HTTP with basic auth are checked.]]></DIAGNOSIS>
        <CONSEQUENCE><![CDATA[A malicious individual can easily intercept unencrypted passwords during transmission using a &quot;network sniffer&quot; and use this data to gain unauthorized access.]]></CONSEQUENCE>
        <SOLUTION><![CDATA[If possible, use alternate services that provide encryption.<BR>
Using strong cryptography, render all authentication credentials (such as passwords/phrases) unreadable during transmission.]]></SOLUTION>
        <RESULT><![CDATA[Service name: TFTP on UDP port 69.]]></RESULT>
      </VULN>
    </CAT>
