      <INFO number="82053" severity="1">
        <TITLE><![CDATA[Host Responds to TCP SYN Packet with Other Flags On with SYN ACK]]></TITLE>
        <LAST_UPDATE><![CDATA[2004-06-25T20:25:28Z]]></LAST_UPDATE>
        <PCI_FLAG>0</PCI_FLAG>
        <DIAGNOSIS><![CDATA[The host responds to a TCP SYN packet with at least one of the following flags set with a SYN ACK packet: RST, FIN, ACK, FIN|PSH.]]></DIAGNOSIS>
        <CONSEQUENCE><![CDATA[This behavior in the TCP/IP implementation may allow a remote user to potentially bypass a firewall protecting the host, as some (especially stateless) firewalls may be configured to allow all TCP packets with one of these flags set (RST, FIN, ACK, FIN|PSH) to go through without examining the packets' SYN flag.]]></CONSEQUENCE>
        <SOLUTION><![CDATA[Many operating systems are known to have this behavior.]]></SOLUTION>
        <RESULT><![CDATA[Host responded to the following TCP probes to port 23 with SYN+ACK:
SYN+RST
SYN+FIN
SYN+ACK]]></RESULT>
