    <CAT value="Web server" port="8008" protocol="tcp">
      <VULN number="86606" severity="2">
        <TITLE><![CDATA[thttpd Web Server Information Disclosure Vulnerability]]></TITLE>
        <LAST_UPDATE><![CDATA[2009-05-05T22:25:19Z]]></LAST_UPDATE>
        <PCI_FLAG>1</PCI_FLAG>
        <DIAGNOSIS><![CDATA[Some versions of the thttpd Web server are vulnerable to an information disclosure vulnerability. When authentication is required, the Web server responds to an HTTP request for an existing file differently than the way it responds to an HTTP request for a non-existing file.]]></DIAGNOSIS>
        <CONSEQUENCE><![CDATA[Successful exploitation of this vulnerability allows an unauthenticated remote user to obtain, via bruteforcing, the names of files that are present on the host.
<P>
When the Web server runs on a special device, this weakness may allow an unauthenticated remote user to fingerprint the device based on the presence of one or more files unique to the device.]]></CONSEQUENCE>
        <SOLUTION><![CDATA[Please contact the vendor for a possible patch for this issue.]]></SOLUTION>
        <RESULT><![CDATA[File /index.html is present.]]></RESULT>
      </VULN>
      <VULN number="86763" severity="2">
