    <CAT value="File Transfer Protocol" port="21" protocol="tcp">
      <PRACTICE number="27114" severity="5" cveid="CVE-2001-1113">
        <TITLE><![CDATA[TrollFTPD Buffer Overflow Vulnerability]]></TITLE>
        <LAST_UPDATE><![CDATA[2009-06-09T09:26:01Z]]></LAST_UPDATE>
        <PCI_FLAG>1</PCI_FLAG>
        <CVE_ID_LIST>
          <CVE_ID>
            <ID><![CDATA[CVE-2001-1113]]></ID>
            <URL><![CDATA[http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2001-1113]]></URL>
          </CVE_ID>
        </CVE_ID_LIST>
        <BUGTRAQ_ID_LIST>
          <BUGTRAQ_ID>
            <ID><![CDATA[3174]]></ID>
            <URL><![CDATA[http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/3174]]></URL>
          </BUGTRAQ_ID>
        </BUGTRAQ_ID_LIST>
        <DIAGNOSIS><![CDATA[<P>TrollFTPD is a small FTP server offered by TrollTech. It contains an exploitable buffer overflow in it's handling of long path names.  The overflow condition occurs when a client requests a recursive directory list. 
<P>If a path greater than 4088 characters in length exists on the filesystem, and a recursive directory list of the long directory is requested, then a stack overrun will corrupt a function stack frame. Malicious users may be able to exploit this vulnerability if they can create directories on the affected FTP servers. They may be able to construct a directory tree with exploit code as part of the path. It's also been demonstrated that it's possible to force the execution of shellcode as root by taking advantage of this vulnerability.]]></DIAGNOSIS>
        <CONSEQUENCE><![CDATA[You should check to make sure that the version you are using is at least Version 1.27. (Note: TrollFTPD does not disclose this information in it's banner.)
<P>If you are using a vulnerable version, then any FTP user who can create a directory on your server can exploit this vulnerability to gain local access to the machine (with the same privileges as the FTPD).]]></CONSEQUENCE>
        <SOLUTION><![CDATA[Upgrade to the newest TrollFTPD, which you can download from the following FTP link:
<P>
<A TARGET="_blank" HREF="ftp://ftp.trolltech.com/freebies/ftpd/">ftp://ftp.trolltech.com/freebies/ftpd/</A>]]></SOLUTION>
        <RESULT><![CDATA[220-Setting memory limit to 1024+1024kbytes
220-Local time is now 11:02 and the load is 0.16.
220 You will be disconnected after 1800 seconds of inactivity.]]></RESULT>
      </PRACTICE>
    </CAT>
  </PRACTICES>
</IP>
